Since bocl is intended to compile CL implementations, they may be
written with various file naming conventions, so we must be adaptable.

For example, for Common Lisp sources, the following file types have been used:

| file-type |
|-----------|
| cl        |
| lisp      |
| lsp       |
| l         |

But others could be possible.

Similarly, for compiled files, several file-types have been used:

| file-type |
|-----------|
| fas       |
| fasl      |

and others.

Also any case is possible for these file types, both cases and mixed
cases are possible, both on case sensitive file systems, and on case
insensitive file systems.

** Variable: BOCL:*SOURCE-FILE-TYPES*

The BOCL:*SOURCE-FILE-TYPES* variable specifies what file-type are
tried to find a source file that is specified without a file-type. The
list contains file-types (strings), or (:case-insensive "file-type").
file-types are taken case sensitively (but remains insensitive on a
case-insensitive file-system). if (:case-insensive "file-type") is
specified, the file type is searched in a case insensitive way even on
a case sensitive file-system.  The first file-type that is found is
used.

When (:case-insensive "file-type") is specified, the order in which
the various options are tried is not specified, apart that the given
"file-type" is tried first.

With a  case-sensitive file-system containing:
| file-namestring |
|-----------------|
| foo.LSP         |
| foo.Lsp         |
| foo.lSp         |
| foo.lsP         |
(:case-insensitive "lsp") could select any of them.


With a  case-sensitive file-system containing:
| file-namestring |
|-----------------|
| foo.LSP         |
| foo.Lsp         |
| foo.lSp         |
| foo.lsP         |
| foo.lsp         |
(:case-insensitive "lsp") would select "foo.lsp" since "lsp" is tried first.

** Variable: BOCL:*COMPILED-FILE-TYPES*

Similarly a BOCL:*COMPILED-FILE-TYPES* list specifies the file-type
expected for compiled files.

** Variable: BOCL:*DEFAULT-COMPILED-FILE-TYPE*

Specifies the default compiled-file type.

** Summary of default values:

| variable                            | default value                              |
|-------------------------------------+--------------------------------------------|
| bocl:*accepted-source-file-types*   | '("lisp" "LISP" (:case-insensitive "lisp") |
|                                     | (:case-insensitive "lsp")                  |
|                                     | (:case-insensitive "cl")                   |
|                                     | (:case-insensitive "l"))                   |
|                                     |                                            |
| bocl:*accepted-compiled-file-types* | '("fasl" "FASL" (:case-insensitive "fasl") |
|                                     | (:case-insensitive "fas")                  |
|                                     | (:case-insensitive "obj")                  |
|                                     | (:case-insensitive "o"))                   |
|                                     |                                            |
| bocl:*default-compiled-file-type*   | "fasl"                                     |
|                                     |                                            |


** LOAD pathname &key …

The following pseudo-codes are applied after merging with *DEFAULT-PATHNAME-DEFAULTS*.

Pseudo code to select the file to load:

#+begin_src lisp
  (cond
    ((pathname has a file-type)
     (do-load pathname))

    ((file at pathname exists)
     (do-load pathname))

    ((file with one of the *accepted-compiled-file-types* is found)
     (if (file with one of the *accepted-source-file-types* is found)
         ;; we have both a .fasl and a .lisp file, we load the more recent one:
         (if (more-recent (file-write-date (file with one of the *accepted-compiled-file-types*))
                          (file-write-date (file with one of the *accepted-source-file-types*)))
             (do-load (file with one of the *accepted-compiled-file-types*))
             (do-load (file with one of the *accepted-source-file-types*)))
         ;; we only have a .fasl file:
         (do-load (file with one of the *accepted-compiled-file-types*))))

    ;; we don't have a .fasl file:
    ((file with one of the *accepted-source-file-types* is found)
     (do-load (file with one of the source-file-type)))

    ;; we don't have a file to load
    (t (error "No file at pathname")))

#+end_src

** COMPILE-FILE source-file &key object-file …

The following pseudo-codes are applied after merging with *DEFAULT-PATHNAME-DEFAULTS*.

Pseudo code to select the file to compile:

#+begin_src lisp
  (cond
    ((pathname has a file-type)
     (do-compile-file pathname))

    ((file at pathname exists)
     (do-compile-file pathname))

    ((file with one of the *accepted-source-file-types* is found)
     (do-compile-file (file with one of the source-file-type)))

    ;; we don't have a file to load
    (t (error "No file at pathname")))
#+end_src

To select the output-file pathname:

If the  output-file pathname is given, then it's used as is.
Otherwise, the output-file pathname is derived from the actual input
file pathname, by replacing the file-type with:
bocl:*default-compiled-file-type*
#+begin_src lisp
(make-pathname :defaults actual-input-pathname :type bocl:*default-compiled-file-type*)
#+end_src

