PROGRESS (slice 44):
- Defined *ACCEPTED-SOURCE-FILE-TYPES*, *ACCEPTED-COMPILED-FILE-TYPES*,
  *DEFAULT-COMPILED-FILE-TYPE* with the specified defaults, plus the
  %FIND-TYPED-FILE helper.  COMPILE-FILE-PATHNAME now uses
  *DEFAULT-COMPILED-FILE-TYPE*.
REMAINING: wire the full LOAD / COMPILE-FILE file-selection pseudocode
(try typed candidates; load the more recent of compiled vs source).

----------------------------------------------------------------------
DONE (slice 47, v1.1.4) — issue resolved, moved to issues/closed.
- LOAD now implements the full file-selection pseudocode (bootstrap/prelude.lisp):
  (1) explicit file-type -> load it; an absent file with a known *compiled*
      file-type falls back to its source sibling (keeps the COMPILE-AND-LOAD
      idiom working, since bocl writes no real fast-load file);
  (2) typeless and the named file exists -> load it;
  (3) typeless -> search *ACCEPTED-COMPILED-FILE-TYPES* and
      *ACCEPTED-SOURCE-FILE-TYPES*; when both a compiled and a source candidate
      exist, load the more recent (FILE-WRITE-DATE); else load whichever exists;
      else honour :IF-DOES-NOT-EXIST.
- COMPILE-FILE now implements its input-selection pseudocode: explicit type or
  an existing file is used as is; otherwise the accepted source file types are
  searched; no source -> error.  Output pathname still derives from
  *DEFAULT-COMPILED-FILE-TYPE* via COMPILE-FILE-PATHNAME.
- New helpers: %FIND-SOURCE-FILE, %FIND-COMPILED-FILE, %KNOWN-FILE-TYPE-P,
  %EXPLICIT-TYPE-P (built on the existing %FIND-TYPED-FILE).
- Verified: lowercase/UPPER/case-insensitive type search; newer-compiled-wins;
  compiled-type fallback to source; .cl/.lsp resolution; :if-does-not-exist nil
  -> NIL; missing -> error; compile-file typeless -> resolves source, returns
  .fasl pathname; compile-file with no source -> error.
